      "created_at": "2018-11-13T17:28:48.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>I'm envisioning a competitive Sentinels of the Multiverse tournament, with meta aspects similar to the Sentinel Tactics tournaments:</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<ul>\n\t<li>Head to head competition between two contestants, probably individuals, but&nbsp;I suppose it could be teams of people, too.</li>\n\t<li>Randomly choose two villains, two environments, and eight heroes. Each contestant&nbsp;will fight the same villain and environment, but which villain/environment pair will be used gets decided by choices made by the contestants. The eight heroes get picked, one at a time, by the two contestants.&nbsp;At least three heroes must be chosen by each contestant, but contestants can continue adding heroes as long as any remain, so the contestants don't have to end up with the same number of heroes.</li>\n\t<li>If one contestant wins their game and the other loses, it's obvious which contestant is the winner of the match, but since&nbsp;SotM is at its core a win or lose game, any method for breaking ties will fundamentally change how the game is played.</li>\n\t<li>So, make the tiebreaker something that is chosen by the contestants. Possible tiebreakers include: Number of rounds, number of turns, Total remaining HP, number of unincapacitated heroes. Those are off the top of my head. I suspect there are others that could be used.</li>\n\t<li>Perhaps if both contestants lose, the match would be repeated with a new set of villains, environments, and heroes.</li>\n\t<li>The coin flip winner can choose either to: A) Decide which villain and environment are used and pick a&nbsp;hero first,&nbsp;or B) Decide which tiebreaker to use and play second.</li>\n\t<li>I'm not sure if it's more interesting to randomly specify the hero and/or villain variants or make those choices the contestants make.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>What do y'all think?&nbsp;</p>\n<p>If people are excited to try this, let me know. I think it would be fun to run a tournament and I think we can do it online.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
